\noindent
An `equality-based' rule of modus ponens holds:

$$
\frac{\Gamma\vdash p;~~~\Delta \vdash p'=q}
{\Gamma\cup \Delta \vdash q}
$$

$$
\frac{\Gamma\vdash p;~~~\Delta \vdash p'=q}
{\Gamma\cup \Delta \vdash q}
$$

$$
\frac{\Gamma \vdash p;~~~\Delta\vdash q}
{(\Gamma\setminus q)\cup (\Delta\setminus p)
\vdash p=q}
$$
